        "company": "Eccam"
      },
      "data": [
        {
          "id": "2",
          "guid": "45659c99-3924-4849-a8ef-805cecce2ba5",
          "text": "<p><em>© Copyright by Eccam s.r.o. All rights reserved.</em></p>",
          "attachments": [
            "INF-2_1_reqview_icon.png"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "21",
          "guid": "d44a3fde-e852-4cd2-bfd7-aaacd6567915",
          "heading": "History",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "22",
              "guid": "a5a4569b-51e3-477c-a8f2-dad3f75467d3",
              "text": "<table style=\"width: 100%;\"><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Date</th><th><strong>Reason for Change</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2015-08-31</td><td style=\"width: 49.899%;\">Initial draft</td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2016-01-14</td><td style=\"width: 49.899%;\">Added document <em>TESTS</em></td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2016-05-27</td><td style=\"width: 49.899%;\">Added document <em>NEEDS</em></td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2016-06-17</td><td style=\"width: 49.899%;\">Added document <em>RISKS</em></td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2017-02-23</td><td style=\"width: 49.899%;\">Reordered documents and other minor updates</td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2018-04-10</td><td style=\"width: 49.899%;\">Added template columns to documents <em>NEEDS</em>, <em>SRS&nbsp;</em>and <em>RISKS</em></td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2018-08-19</td><td style=\"width: 49.899%;\">Added document <em>INF&nbsp;</em>with overall description</td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2018-11-16</td><td style=\"width: 49.899%;\">Added column <em>Upstream Traceability&nbsp;</em>to document <em>SRS</em></td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2019-05-19</td><td style=\"width: 49.899%;\">Aligned documents <em>SRS&nbsp;</em>with the ISO/IEC/IEEE 29148 template</td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2019-09-12</td><td style=\"width: 49.899%;\">Added document <em>ARCH</em></td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2019-10-23</td><td style=\"width: 49.899%;\">Simplified traceability columns to contain only formatting recognized by MS Word in the exported output</td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Tom Novacek</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2020-06-24</td><td style=\"width: 49.899%;\">Updated Introduction section in all documents</td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2022-04-24</td><td>Added type attribute to documents <em>TESTS</em> and&nbsp;<em>ARCH</em>.<br>Added <em>usage&nbsp;</em>traceability links in document <em>ARCH</em></td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2023-05-17</td><td>Organized documents in groups<br>Defined table views</td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2024-03-08</td><td>Added document <em>ASVS</em><br>Added security requirements document <em>SRS</em></td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 19.1686%; text-align: center;\">Libor Bus</td><td style=\"width: 30.7071%; text-align: center;\">2025-06-04</td><td>Added project dashboard<br>Added new user stories describing Jira and EA integrations to document NEEDS<br>Added new requirements describing Jira and EA integrations to document SRS<br></td></tr></tbody></table><p><br></p>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "1",
          "guid": "cb0dfa58-adc6-42e9-beea-5c3541a0cf29",
          "heading": "Introduction",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "10",
              "guid": "43f1b471-570f-40cb-aeed-d230beeb414b",
              "heading": "Purpose",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "13",
                  "guid": "ae2f412c-521b-4fd5-94b4-34d227352b64",
                  "text": "<p><span style=\"text-align: start;\">The main purpose of this project is to provide new&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://reqview.com\" style=\"text-align: start;\">ReqView&nbsp;</a><span style=\"text-align: start;\">users a working example how to specify and manage requirements for a SW product.</span></p>"
                },
                {
                  "id": "12",
                  "guid": "0d034daa-b479-49a3-b9c8-94726c550721",
                  "text": "<p>This project specifies basic functionality of<span style=\"text-align: start;\">&nbsp;a simple&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples\" style=\"text-align: start;\">HW/SW requirements management tool</a><span style=\"text-align: start;\">.&nbsp;</span>It describes user needs, information security requirements, risks, low level SW requirements, verification and SW architecture.</p><p><strong>Note:</strong> The project is not complete.</p>"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "11",
              "guid": "2e31f9b5-d2f7-4d42-900a-0dc9e60629fd",
              "heading": "Intended Audience",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "14",
                  "guid": "f9b4cec7-e383-4bed-8496-3c6793f4056f",
                  "text": "<p>The target audience are new ReqView users evaluating ReqView and users learning how to gather and manage requirements in ReqView.</p>"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "25",
              "guid": "4aff0011-6393-46fc-a362-dcbf8f30db04",
              "heading": "Project Structure",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "9",
                  "guid": "c34f63fa-d24d-48dc-992e-51581da51043",
                  "attachments": [
                    "INF-9_1_Project Traceability Diagram.png"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "3",
          "guid": "37c768e3-641f-4989-bb46-1260e4edc7a8",
          "heading": "Documents",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "27",
              "guid": "5385af5b-7eca-4e57-9245-e1e52ce90a24",
              "heading": "Level 1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "5",
                  "guid": "100123cb-1d16-419f-a305-90bf4524ee86",
                  "heading": "NEEDS: ReqView User Needs",
                  "text": "<p><em>NEEDS</em> document describes the highest level <em>user stories</em> and <em>constraints</em>.</p>",
                  "links": {
                    "reference": [
                      "NEEDS-3",
                      "NEEDS-4"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "30",
                  "guid": "54fd60eb-7867-45f4-94e9-6ff5b21a1e58",
                  "heading": "ASVS: OWASP Application Security Verification Standard",
                  "text": "<p>ASVS document describes application <em>security requirements</em>.</p>",
                  "links": {
                    "reference": [
                      "ASVS-61",
                      "ASVS-118",
                      "ASVS-186",
                      "ASVS-214",
                      "ASVS-228",
                      "ASVS-264",
                      "ASVS-285",
                      "ASVS-303",
                      "ASVS-324",
                      "ASVS-335",
                      "ASVS-349",
                      "ASVS-359",
                      "ASVS-381",
                      "ASVS-401"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "8",
                  "guid": "c87fe938-b654-4b0c-85da-e1b949d13dcb",
                  "heading": "RISKS: Failure Mode and Effects Analysis",
                  "text": "<p><em>RISKS</em> document describes project risks using <em>failure mode and effects analysis</em> (FMEA) method.</p>",
                  "links": {
                    "reference": [
                      "RISKS-2"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "28",
              "guid": "bd22db9e-ccd4-48dc-972a-6f69c23287d4",
              "heading": "Level 2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "6",
                  "guid": "56158b1c-4c64-4a44-b048-c7b402c96df3",
                  "heading": "SRS: ReqView Software Requirements Specification",
                  "text": "<p><em>SRS</em> document describes <em>SW requirements</em> derived from user stories or mitigating project risks.</p>",
                  "links": {
                    "reference": [
                      "SRS-20"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "7",
                  "guid": "2bfcd9e6-3de4-4495-b27d-9f851f088edf",
                  "heading": "TESTS: ReqView Verification Tests",
                  "text": "<p><em>TESTS</em> document describes <em>test cases</em> verifying functionality described by the SW requirements.</p>",
                  "links": {
                    "reference": [
                      "TESTS-2"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "29",
              "guid": "e81e2fc9-587c-4631-80e5-527808a75ccd",
              "heading": "Level 3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "23",
                  "guid": "cb66b166-cfe7-4352-90f7-1bbc3a492973",
                  "heading": "ARCH: ReqView Architecture",
                  "text": "<p><em>ARCH</em> document describes the architecture of the application described by the SW requirements.</p>",
                  "links": {
                    "reference": [
                      "ARCH-2"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "4",
          "guid": "dc3049f9-b025-4e6d-ac12-85e9e90b4e77",
          "heading": "Traceability",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "16",
              "guid": "69884407-27d6-40ea-9a43-362c075a2441",
              "heading": "Satisfaction Links",
              "text": "<p>Satisfaction links lead from downstream SW requirements to the related highest level user needs and security requirements (M:N).</p>"
            },
            {
              "id": "20",
              "guid": "51ea8c7d-5985-4151-b559-91de5c8434df",
              "heading": "Mitigation Links",
              "text": "<p>Mitigation links lead from downstream SW requirements to the related project risk corrective actions (M:N).</p>"
            },
            {
              "id": "17",
              "guid": "ee02f69d-0255-43e2-9cb6-4ecfe30566f3",
              "heading": "Verification Links",
              "text": "<p>Verification links lead from a test case to the related SW requirements (M:N).</p>"
            },
            {
              "id": "24",
              "guid": "e7a4cd8b-0294-4632-a3b2-ceeb0c0da55f",
              "heading": "Implementation Links",
              "text": "<p>Implementation links lead from a component in the architecture to the relates SW requirements (M:N).</p>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "attributes": {
