        "format": "2.22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "NEEDS",
      "guid": "cf024593-2de0-45cf-ae98-0941b85cc094",
      "name": "ReqView User Needs",
      "lastId": 84,
      "createdOn": "2016-05-24T09:16:13.126Z",
      "createdBy": {
        "name": "Libor Bus",
        "email": "libor.bus@eccam.com",
        "company": "Eccam s.r.o."
      },
      "lastChangedOn": "2025-06-04T14:35:37.733Z",
      "lastChangedBy": {
        "name": "Libor Bus",
        "email": "libor.bus@eccam.com",
        "company": "Eccam"
      },
      "data": [
        {
          "id": "45",
          "guid": "57916083-61b1-4406-b5ec-a341a2c10de7",
          "text": "<p><em>© Copyright by Eccam s.r.o. All rights reserved.</em></p>",
          "type": "INF"
        },
        {
          "id": "2",
          "guid": "c41769d3-cac5-4c45-9dfa-a33f52ac93d6",
          "heading": "Introduction",
          "instructions": "<p>This document describes needs of product stakeholders as agile <em>user stories</em>. User stories are simple statements formulated according to the following template:</p><p>“<em>As a</em> &lt;type of user&gt;, <em>I want</em> &lt;some goal&gt;, <em>so that</em> &lt;some reason&gt;.”</p><p>For more information see <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/User-Stories-Applied-Software-Development/dp/0321205685\">User Stories Applied</a> by Mike Cohn or his <a href=\"https://www.mountaingoatsoftware.com/agile/user-stories\">User Stories</a> web page.</p>",
          "type": "SEC",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "64",
              "guid": "9b0d3723-912b-4728-aa0e-5c3bdfe04ea0",
              "heading": "Purpose",
              "instructions": "<p>Identify the product specified in this document.</p>",
              "type": "SEC",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "67",
                  "guid": "05fa03f6-9896-41cf-abc5-05c567b3cbbd",
                  "text": "<p>The main purpose of this document is to provide new <a href=\"https://reqview.com\">ReqView&nbsp;</a>users a working example of a document describing high-level user needs by means of user stories.</p>",
                  "type": "INF"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "65",
              "guid": "8f30721e-0740-4277-b997-427a6b7e6db7",
              "heading": "Scope",
              "instructions": "<p>Briefly describe the scope of the product.</p>",
              "type": "SEC",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "75",
                  "guid": "1b5b7ed0-1303-41e7-a58b-87e40e495784",
                  "text": "<p>This document specifies top level user needs for a simple <a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples\">HW/SW requirements management tool</a>.</p><p><strong>Note:</strong> The document is not complete.</p>",
                  "type": "INF"
                },
                {
                  "id": "66",
                  "guid": "7b6ac21f-da50-47b3-bf72-b31a5fee2331",
                  "text": "<p>Users should be able to:</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/edit-document/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples\">Capture requirements specifications</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/edit-document/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples#edit-attributes\">Manage requirements using custom attributes</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/requirements-traceability-links/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples\">Set up requirements traceability</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/blog/requirements-traceability-matrix/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples#traceability-matrix\">Browse the requirements traceability matrix (RTM)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/change-management/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples#control-project-changes\">Control project changes</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/filter-and-search/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples#filter-document-objects\">Filter</a> <a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/review-document/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples\">and search requirements</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/import-html-ms-word/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples\">Import requirements from MS Word</a> or <a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/import-csv-ms-excel/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples\">Excel</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/export-docx/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples\">Export requirements to DOCX</a>, <a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/export-xlsx/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples\">XLSX</a>, <a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/export-pdf/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples\">PDF</a>, <a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/export-html/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples\">HTML</a>, or <a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/export-csv/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples\">CSV</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/requirements-traceability-links/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples#traceability-reports\">Analyze requirements coverage and impact of changes</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/doc/review-document/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples#print-documents\">Print requirements specifications</a></li><li>Integrate ReqView with Jira project management tool&nbsp;</li><li>Integrate ReqView with Enterprise Architect modelling tool</li></ul>",
                  "type": "INF"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "1",
              "guid": "03658799-6c3b-44fe-a0e6-a23613fce43f",
              "heading": "User Roles",
              "instructions": "<p>Identify user roles for the product and for each role describe characteristics of a typical user.</p><p>You may consider creating personas with a real name. Each persona should be described sufficiently that everyone on the team feels like they know the persona.</p>",
              "type": "SEC",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "5",
                  "guid": "2f415d73-2069-4cc2-b2e9-c5b5c359efd2",
                  "heading": "Requirements Architect",
                  "text": "<p>Requirements Architect defines requirements model and configure the requirements project for other users.</p><p>Requirements Architect is typically a <em>QA manager</em> or <em>project manager</em>.</p>",
                  "asAn": "Architect",
                  "iWant": "<ul><li>Define custom attributes</li><li>Configure project traceability</li><li>Create document templates</li></ul>",
                  "type": "INF"
                },
                {
                  "id": "6",
                  "guid": "24d3fba9-b865-41bd-9126-b0aac6f560f0",
                  "heading": "Editor",
                  "text": "<p>Editor defines project requirements and creates requirements and tests documents.</p><p>Editor is typically a <em>requirements engineer</em>, <em>business analyst</em>, <em>project manager</em>, <em>QA engineer</em> or a <em>tester</em>.</p>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<ul><li>Capture structured requirements</li><li>Update requirements custom attributes</li><li>Discuss requirements</li><li>Maintain requirements traceability links</li><li>Print requirements</li><li>Import requirements</li><li>Export requirements</li><li>Create traceability reports</li></ul>",
                  "type": "INF"
                },
                {
                  "id": "7",
                  "guid": "aa5e2cab-0621-4555-bcb7-bf0aeca0394a",
                  "heading": "Reviewer",
                  "text": "<p>Reviewer reads project documents, performs review and provides feedback for improving the content of the document.</p><p>Reviewer is typically an internal <em>QA expert</em> reviewing requirements and tests, <em>customer</em> or <em>supplier</em> commenting requirements and setting the requirement acceptance state.</p>",
                  "asAn": "Reviewer",
                  "iWant": "<ul><li>Provide feedback to requirements specifications</li><li>Update requirements review status</li><li>Print requirements</li></ul>",
                  "type": "INF"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "3",
          "guid": "11f269ac-d037-495b-b873-005baf3b08d0",
          "heading": "User Stories",
          "instructions": "<p>Specify user stories describing functionality of the product grouped into <em>epics</em> for easier navigation in the document.</p><p>Set the following attributes for each story:</p><ul><li><em>Heading:</em> short story name,</li><li><em>As a(n):</em> type of user,</li><li><em>I Want:</em> some goal,</li><li><em>So that:</em> some reason,</li><li><em>Acceptance Criteria:</em> more details how the story should be verified and providing the basic criteria that can be used to determine if a story is fully implemented,</li><li><em>Priority:</em> “High” for fundamental features, “Medium” for important features having a short-term workaround, “Low” for features which can be left out of the release if time runs out or won't-have for features will be needed in a later release,</li><li><em>Risk:</em> “High”, “Medium”, or “Low”,</li><li><em>Estimation:</em> story points which are relative estimate of the complexity, effort or duration of a story, and</li><li><em>Status:</em> workflow information classifying stories as “New”, “Planned”, “Implemented” or “Verified”.</li></ul>",
          "type": "SEC",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "9",
              "guid": "3fb4ac96-1467-4651-99f0-150c6ded802f",
              "heading": "Requirements Storage",
              "type": "EPIC",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "58",
                  "guid": "ab4826dd-421a-40ad-9aea-6c24cf9d0f9c",
                  "heading": "Document Files",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>saving project in a file</li><li>opening project from a file</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>save document in a file</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>users can open the document for further editing or review</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "14",
                  "guid": "d1fa5338-44e6-40e2-a971-b8a656238a16",
                  "heading": "Document Templates",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>saving a document as a document template file,</li><li>add a new document into a project from a saved document template file while preserving document attributes definition, values of object attributes and object attachments.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Architect",
                  "iWant": "<p>save a document as a template file</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can reuse the document structure and configuration of custom attributes for new documents</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "33",
                  "guid": "6c0a35fc-d7f9-4175-84dc-4e5aad145238",
                  "heading": "Autosave",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool:</p><ul><li>instantly saves all the changes,</li><li>restores the same project content when it is restarted.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>automatically persist my changes</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I do not lose my changes if the tool is unexpectedly terminated before saving into a file</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "8",
              "guid": "4883987f-6c3a-4a66-a44f-8cd7000b70f0",
              "heading": "Define Requirements",
              "type": "EPIC",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "68",
                  "guid": "47e4b317-17f5-45c4-a16c-a5fbda44a5c5",
                  "heading": "Requirement Description",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>setting a description of a selected requirement</li><li>removing description of a selected requirement</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>specify requirements by a textual description</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>the requirements can be reviewed by other users.</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "32",
                  "guid": "8366a026-3158-443b-a759-fe299e589534",
                  "heading": "Unique IDs",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>automatic generation of document ID which can not be further changed</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>identify requirements by their unique ID</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can reference requirements from other documents or communication</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "12",
                  "guid": "767f4667-4b3e-497f-b061-6024977a62db",
                  "heading": "Document Structure",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>creation of a new project,</li><li>adding a new document into a project,</li><li>deletion of a document from a project.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>organize requirements in a tree document hierarchy with numbered sections</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can easily navigate in the document structure</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "73",
                  "guid": "b2f883b8-769e-4aeb-b419-41490e5b2ce7",
                  "heading": "Table View",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>displaying of requirements in a table,</li><li>displaying requirements ID, description, discussion, links and custom attributes in columns,</li><li>hiding requirements table columns,</li><li>reordering of requirements table columns,</li><li>resizing of requirements table columns.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>display a table of requirements</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can review all requirements information in a single view</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "74",
                  "guid": "138a88a8-b347-4835-8f85-661236e4c2bd",
                  "heading": "Detailed View",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>displaying custom attributes of the selected requirement in a pane or dialog,</li><li>displaying discussion of the selected requirement in a pane or dialog,</li><li>displaying traceability links for the selected requirement in a pane or dialog,</li><li>displaying history of changes for the selected requirement in a pane or dialog.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>display all information about the selected requirement</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can display details about any requirement which are not visible in the requirements table</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "17",
                  "guid": "40f3c5d5-6c6f-45c6-869a-535b8eadc13a",
                  "heading": "Attachments",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>attachment of image file to document objects,</li><li>displaying image attachments in the context of the related document object,</li><li>deletion of attachments</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>attach images and other documents to requirements</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can enhance textual requirements with visual content such as mockups, diagrams, etc.</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "35",
                  "guid": "7c634ae1-0e07-46c4-bc0c-3340513f6956",
                  "heading": "Sort",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports sorting requirements by:</p><ul><li>the natural document order,</li><li>value of a custom attribute.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>order requirements by a chosen custom attribute</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can display requirements sorted by priority, risk, effort, etc.</p>",
                  "status": "Planned",
                  "type": "STORY"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "70",
              "guid": "ce912e6b-e263-4c69-8d4c-d7d7050ee86b",
              "heading": "Manage Requirements",
              "type": "EPIC",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "19",
                  "guid": "561c6863-ba20-41ef-8f9a-932b8e352af9",
                  "heading": "Custom Attributes Configuration",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>creation of a new custom attribute,</li><li>deletion of a custom attribute,</li><li>definition of following custom attribute types<ul><li>number</li><li>date</li><li>boolean</li><li>single and multivalue enumeration</li><li>string / rich formatted text</li></ul></li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Architect",
                  "iWant": "<p>define additional requirements attributes</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>the document can flexibly store additional requirement properties, such as requirement source, priority, status, etc.</p>",
                  "status": "Verified",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "69",
                  "guid": "8547cf35-70e0-47e9-8683-44702395341a",
                  "heading": "Custom Attributes",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>setting requirements source, priority, status and acceptance criteria</li><li>setting and resetting a value of a custom attribute for multiple requirements</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>set a value of a chosen custom attribute for one or more selected requirements</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can define additional requirements properties, such as requirements source, prioritize requirements, manage requirement status, define acceptance criteria, etc.</p>",
                  "status": "Verified",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "16",
                  "guid": "b9d27d67-aa41-4d85-8cc1-a90a715f9d37",
                  "heading": "Traceability Configuration",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>creation of at least one link type</li><li>definition of a start and end role for a link type</li><li>removal of a link type including all existing links</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Architect",
                  "iWant": "<p>define types of relationships between requirements</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>users can perform traceability analysis for a chosen group of links</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "21",
                  "guid": "d080f428-cf1e-4919-89db-a8169d735e51",
                  "heading": "Traceability Links",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>creation of links with chosen link type between selected requirements,</li><li>deletion of links</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>link related requirements</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can analyze requirements coverage, gap in requirements and impact of requirement changes.</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "34",
                  "guid": "00ab0f5f-5bca-4635-9854-0de89db36a60",
                  "heading": "Filter",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports filtering requirements:</p><ul><li>by full text search in the object heading, text or a custom attribute</li><li>with the given traceability link type</li><li>in the given section</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>filter requirements</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can identify and manipulate requirements matching a condition</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "36",
                  "guid": "f83fb577-55a7-476b-8ea4-83fecdf77f9b",
                  "heading": "Search",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports searching requirements containing a given keyword.</p>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>find keywords</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can identify and manipulate requirements containing the searched keyword(s)</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "22",
              "guid": "fb861b9d-011e-4046-8f17-cdc453bc3ed3",
              "heading": "Review Requirements",
              "type": "EPIC",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "24",
                  "guid": "48d5aa49-31b8-4ff9-a52c-be80258fa9fa",
                  "heading": "Discussion",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>commenting a selected requirement,</li><li>displaying discussion for a selected requirement.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Reviewer",
                  "iWant": "<p>comment requirements</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can provide feedback during requirements review</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "30",
                  "guid": "78da2553-a8ba-47ed-8382-e8c207c1bf4f",
                  "heading": "Traceability Browser",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>displaying linked requirements ordered by link type</li><li>changing focus to a selected requirement</li><li>filtering requirements with missing traceability links of a given link type</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Reviewer",
                  "iWant": "<p>trace related requirements</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can perform coverage, gap and change impact analysis</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "29",
                  "guid": "eea2a384-27ee-44c6-bbd2-6c80a1642768",
                  "heading": "Print",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>printing a document with the same layout as it is displayed,</li><li>saving the document as PDF with the same layout as it is displayed.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Reviewer",
                  "iWant": "<p>print a document view</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can review requirements without the need to run the tool</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "31",
              "guid": "e995cf73-40dd-41da-a96c-141d850cbd85",
              "heading": "Audit Trail",
              "type": "EPIC",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "26",
                  "guid": "92f9a2c4-44fb-49ee-bc72-a5a7110bcd84",
                  "heading": "History of Changes",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>displaying history of changes for a selected requirement.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>list all requirement changes</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can understand how the requirement evolved in time</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "23",
                  "guid": "dd4efc4c-c48c-4723-8866-16999d813d7f",
                  "heading": "Traceability Report",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>generation of a custom traceability report which visualizes end-to-end requirements traceability</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Reviewer",
                  "iWant": "<p>generate a traceability report</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can analyze coverage, gaps and impact of requirements changes</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "11",
              "guid": "fd49a637-753e-4114-8caa-587db1bea80b",
              "heading": "Integrations",
              "type": "EPIC",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "27",
                  "guid": "f267ba72-6383-44b1-8b6a-37422d3841a4",
                  "heading": "Import from Word",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>import of MS Word HTML preserving structure of document sections and paragraphs and image attachments</li><li>pasting of a text or a HTML fragment to requirements description.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>import a requirements specification from a MS Word document</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can reuse existing requirements specifications or other structured documents</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "71",
                  "guid": "c511a76d-8c3c-4643-a24c-5124ba36df3a",
                  "heading": "Import from Excel",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>import of new requirements from a CSV file including custom attribute values</li><li>updating requirements from a CSV file including custom attribute values</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>import requirements from a MS Excel spreadsheet</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can import or update list of requirements</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "28",
                  "guid": "a71a2a78-a185-43e7-891b-34b3247e93bc",
                  "heading": "Export to Word",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>export of a document to a HTML file,</li><li>import of an exported HTML file to a MS Word document preserving requirements structure and content</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>to export structured requirements specification to MS Word</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can share requirements specifications with users without the tool</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "72",
                  "guid": "6ac4abc9-e72b-4e19-9412-80fe38121ec5",
                  "heading": "Export to CSV",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>export of filtered list of requirements to a CSV file.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>export filtered list of requirements to MS Excel</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can reuse or update requirements in another application</p>",
                  "status": "Implemented",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "80",
                  "guid": "a73d14ba-8b96-4f87-9a62-2f3089395772",
                  "heading": "Export to Jira",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>export of requirements from a document to Jira,</li><li>mapping type of requirements to Jira work types,</li><li>setting Jira work item summary, description from ReqView id, heading and text attributes,</li><li>preserving values of other Jira work item fields updated by Jira users (iteration, owner, status),</li><li>preserving Jira links,</li><li>bidirectional navigation between exported ReqView requirements and corresponding Jira work items.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>export requirements to Jira</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>the development team can manage requirements implementation</p>",
                  "status": "Planned",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "81",
                  "guid": "9830280e-05a6-487e-bb93-83ae4b2005f6",
                  "heading": "Update from Jira",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>mapping Jira work item fields to ReqView attributes,</li><li>updating values of mapped attributes from corresponding Jira work item fields.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>update requirements by information from Jira</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can track the implementation status in ReqView&nbsp;</p>",
                  "status": "Planned",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "84",
                  "guid": "d7779470-dc1c-421a-8de7-40cd8671e614",
                  "heading": "Export to ReqIF",
                  "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool supports:</p><ul><li>exporting documents to the ReqIF format,</li><li>preserving requirements structure, format, attachments, attributes, and links between exported requirements,</li><li>compliance with <a href=\"https://www.omg.org/reqif/\">OMG ReqIF standard</a>.</li></ul>",
                  "asAn": "Editor",
                  "iWant": "<p>export document to &nbsp;the Requirements Interchange Format (ReqIF)</p>",
                  "soThat": "<p>I can provide requirements in a standardized format to suppliers or other team members using other tools</p>",
                  "status": "Planned",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "82",
                  "guid": "97181f13-30c7-427d-8bc3-a2a8ba556b08",
                  "heading": "Export to Enterprise Architect",
                  "status": "New",
                  "type": "STORY"
                },
                {
                  "id": "83",
                  "guid": "24e864b2-5105-4712-b09a-ce981c8f6e04",
                  "heading": "Import from Enterprise Architect",
                  "status": "New",
                  "type": "STORY"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "4",
          "guid": "fc5a0688-ffa0-4d49-8f88-f6cb7ebe15c1",
          "heading": "Constraints",
          "type": "SEC",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "39",
              "guid": "03711176-9aac-4767-a58f-a9238495d0c4",
              "heading": "Startup Time",
              "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool starts in less than 10s even for large projects.</p>",
              "asAn": "Editor",
              "iWant": "<p>quickly start the tool</p>",
              "soThat": "<p>I do not need to wait long time for editing a project</p>",
              "status": "Verified",
              "type": "CON"
            },
            {
              "id": "41",
              "guid": "4cb8d2ca-d47c-4666-8551-e8fb663c1667",
              "heading": "Edit Response Time",
              "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool updates view after any edit operation in a document with 10000 requirements in less than 1s.</p>",
              "asAn": "Editor",
              "iWant": "<p>edit effectively requirements in large documents</p>",
              "soThat": "<p>I can work without waiting for tool responses</p>",
              "status": "Verified",
              "type": "CON"
            },
            {
              "id": "44",
              "guid": "c6d0adc9-ba8d-4f81-bb50-7199c07707fb",
              "heading": "Document Size",
              "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool can store documents with 10000 requirements and 100 attachments of total size 100 MB.</p>",
              "asAn": "Editor",
              "iWant": "<p>create large requirements specifications</p>",
              "soThat": "<p>I can capture all requirements in a single document even for complex system development projects</p>",
              "status": "Verified",
              "type": "CON"
            },
            {
              "id": "42",
              "guid": "0264ef81-e5e4-405f-8dde-4dd74e8721a2",
              "heading": "Security",
              "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool does not send any project information to the internet without user consent.</p>",
              "asAn": "Editor",
              "iWant": "<p>store confidential information in the tool</p>",
              "soThat": "<p>I can be sure that no confidential information is compromised</p>",
              "status": "Verified",
              "type": "CON"
            },
            {
              "id": "51",
              "guid": "12b51945-516b-46fe-991c-5980dc57d099",
              "heading": "Compatibility",
              "acceptanceCriteria": "<p>Tool is installed and run on Windows, Linux and a Mac.</p>",
              "asAn": "Editor",
              "iWant": "<p>install and run the tool on Windows, Linux or Mac operating system</p>",
              "soThat": "<p>I can use the tool on any desktop PC or notebook.</p>",
              "status": "Verified",
              "type": "CON"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "attributes": {
        "acceptanceCriteria": {
          "name": "Acceptance Criteria",
          "type": "xhtml"
        },
        "asAn": {
          "name": "As a(n)",
          "type": "enum",
          "values": [
            {
              "key": "Architect"
            },
            {
