    {
      "id": "RISKS",
      "guid": "d1767ebc-7332-4fa9-bdc7-a8ad00ad2c83",
      "name": "Failure Mode and Effects Analysis",
      "lastId": 46,
      "createdOn": "2016-06-16T13:26:33.494Z",
      "createdBy": {
        "name": "Libor Bus",
        "email": "libor.bus@eccam.com",
        "company": "Eccam s.r.o."
      },
      "lastChangedOn": "2025-06-04T14:35:02.250Z",
      "lastChangedBy": {
        "name": "Libor Bus",
        "email": "libor.bus@eccam.com",
        "company": "Eccam"
      },
      "data": [
        {
          "id": "10",
          "guid": "f38197a5-9d15-4a0b-bb95-e684a6e3acad",
          "text": "<p><em>© Copyright by Eccam s.r.o. All rights reserved.</em></p>",
          "type": "INF"
        },
        {
          "id": "1",
          "guid": "132dcab5-8b8b-46c0-ab37-e3752aab1331",
          "heading": "Introduction",
          "instructions": "<p>This document describes product or process failures using <em>Failure Mode and Effects Analysis</em> (FMEA) method.</p><p>You can identify potential <em>failure modes</em>, their <em>causes</em>, and <em>effects</em> on the system or stakeholders.</p><p>For each identified cause and effect you can assess its <em>risk</em> and determine <em>corrective actions</em>.</p><p>For more information see <a href=\"http://www.effectivefmeas.com/\">Effective FMEAs</a> by Carl Carlson.</p>",
          "type": "SEC",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "5",
              "guid": "a85e7603-54d0-41ab-aa96-fd4f20dc2720",
              "heading": "Purpose",
              "instructions": "<p>Identify the product specified in this document.</p>",
              "type": "SEC",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "36",
                  "guid": "0f545e62-d6b0-4c2c-b6f6-1b4a3905327c",
                  "text": "<p>The main purpose of this document is to provide new ReqView users a working example of a document describing project risks by means of <em>Failure Mode and Effects Analysis</em> (FMEA) method.</p>",
                  "type": "INF"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "27",
              "guid": "6dda73cb-48b7-4ea8-9ff0-585187c2f4df",
              "heading": "Scope",
              "instructions": "<p>Briefly describe the scope of the product risk analysis.</p>",
              "type": "SEC",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "28",
                  "guid": "fb943a0f-aaa4-4cda-a2de-b7643af054aa",
                  "text": "<p>This document describes risks related to development of <span style=\"text-align: start;\">a simple&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.reqview.com/?utm_source=WebApp&amp;utm_medium=Application&amp;utm_campaign=Examples\" style=\"text-align: start;\">HW/SW requirements management tool</a> as specified in the document <em>[DEMO-NEEDS]</em>.</p><p><strong>Note:</strong> The document is not complete.</p>",
                  "type": "INF"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "30",
              "guid": "45b82e0f-8430-41ab-9630-7ab0d692acf1",
              "heading": "Definitions",
              "type": "SEC",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "35",
                  "guid": "400a777f-4ba0-44d8-bc2d-b25513feea0f",
                  "text": "<p>This section provides example definitions of <em>probability</em>, <em>severability</em> and <em>detectability</em> taken from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Failure_mode_and_effects_analysis\">Wikipedia</a>.</p>",
                  "type": "INF"
                },
                {
                  "id": "32",
                  "guid": "42dcfdef-e805-4e70-bb81-2221b59ba4de",
                  "text": "<p><strong>Severity:</strong></p><table><thead><tr><th>Rating</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1-2</td><td>No relevant effect on reliability or safety</td></tr><tr><td>3-4</td><td>Very minor, no damage, no injuries, only results in a maintenance action (only noticed by discriminating customers)</td></tr><tr><td>5-6</td><td>Minor, low damage, light injuries (affects very little of the system, noticed by average customer)</td></tr><tr><td>7-8</td><td>Critical (causes a loss of primary function; Loss of all safety Margins, 1 failure away from a catastrophe, severe damage, severe injuries, max 1 possible death )</td></tr><tr><td>9-10</td><td>Catastrophic (product becomes inoperative; the failure may result in complete unsafe operation and possible multiple deaths)</td></tr></tbody></table>",
                  "instructions": "<p>Define rank for severity from 1 (no effect) up to 10 (catastrophic) used further in the document, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Failure_mode_and_effects_analysis#Severity_.28S.29\">see example</a>.</p>",
                  "type": "INF"
                },
                {
                  "id": "31",
                  "guid": "1e1544d3-9614-4138-886b-b42392300336",
                  "text": "<p><strong>Probability:</strong></p><table><thead><tr><th>Rating</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1-2</td><td>Extremely Unlikely (Virtually impossible or No known occurrences on similar products or processes, with many running hours)</td></tr><tr><td>3-4</td><td>Remote (relatively few failures)</td></tr><tr><td>5-6</td><td>Occasional (occasional failures)</td></tr><tr><td>7-8</td><td>Reasonably Possible (repeated failures)</td></tr><tr><td>9-10</td><td>Frequent (failure is almost inevitable)</td></tr></tbody></table>",
                  "instructions": "<p>Define rank for probability from 1 (extremely unlikely) to 10 (inevitable) used further in the document, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Failure_mode_and_effects_analysis#Probability_.28P.29\">see example</a>.</p>",
                  "type": "INF"
                },
                {
                  "id": "33",
                  "guid": "3cbd0c5e-e1ff-4e92-8ed6-90d22c2d3bc7",
                  "text": "<p><strong>Detectability:</strong></p><table><thead><tr><th>Rating</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Certain – fault will be caught on test - e.g. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poka-yoke\">Poka-Yoke</a></td></tr><tr><td>2-3</td><td>Almost certain</td></tr><tr><td>4-5</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>6-7</td><td>Moderate</td></tr><tr><td>8-9</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Fault is undetected by Operators or Maintainers</td></tr></tbody></table>",
                  "instructions": "<p>Define rank for detection from 1 (almost certain) up to 10 (absolute uncertainly) used further in the document, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Failure_mode_and_effects_analysis#Detection_.28D.29\">see example</a>.</p>",
                  "type": "INF"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "2",
          "guid": "226aa626-520e-47a1-b4ed-3981c7d2617c",
          "heading": "Risks",
          "instructions": "<p>Identify potential failure modes, their causes, and effects on the system or stakeholders. For each identified cause and effect assess its risk and determine <em>corrective actions</em>. For more information see <a href=\"http://www.effectivefmeas.com/\">Effective FMEAs</a> by Carl Carlson.</p><p>Organize failures by items or process step into sections with the following hierarchy: <em>Function</em> → <em>Failure Mode</em> → <em>Potential Cause</em> → <em>Corrective Action</em>.</p><p><strong>Function</strong></p><ul><li><em>Type:</em> set to \"Function\" value</li><li><em>Description:</em> describe the functionality of the item or process</li></ul><p><strong>Failure Modes</strong></p><ul><li><em>Type:</em> set to \"Failure Mode\" value</li><li><em>Description:</em> describe the failure</li><li><em>Potential Effects:</em> describe potential impact of the failure on the system or users</li><li><em>SEV:</em> rate severity of potential effects as a number from 1 (least severe) to 10 (most severe)</li></ul><p><strong>Potential Cause</strong></p><ul><li><em>Type:</em> set to \"Potential Cause\" value</li><li><em>Description:</em> describe the potential cause</li><li><em>SEV:</em> rate severity of potential effects as a number from 1 (least severe) to 10 (most severe)</li><li><em>PROB:</em> rate probability of the cause as a number from 1 (least likely) to 10 (most likely)</li><li><em>Detection Mode:</em> describe existing design controls detecting the cause or preventing the failure from occurring</li><li><em>DET:</em> rate detectability of the cause as a number from1 (best detectable) to 10 (least detectable)</li></ul><p><strong>Corrective Actions</strong></p><ul><li><em>Type:</em> set to \"Corrective Action\" value</li><li><em>Description:</em> describe the action for reducing the occurrence of the cause or improving the detection</li><li><em>Potential Effects:</em> describe potential impact of the failure on the system or users after the corrective action is applied</li><li><em>SEV:</em> rate new severity of the failure effects as a number from 1 (least severe) to 10 (most severe)</li><li><em>Detection Mode:</em> describe how the action improves design controls detecting the failure or preventing the failure from occurring</li><li><em>DET:</em> rate new detectability of the failure as a number from 1 (best detectable) to 10 (least detectable)</li><li><em>Responsibility:</em> name the responsible person</li><li><em>Target Date:</em> plan the action</li></ul>",
          "type": "SEC",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "43",
              "guid": "cf692a0d-ca97-429d-aff0-51b12cd11b8a",
              "heading": "Application",
              "type": "SEC",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "8",
                  "guid": "a7331330-364e-4c3a-8a0c-c964ecdfd359",
                  "text": "<p>Application is reliable</p>",
                  "type": "FUNC",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "22",
                      "guid": "c6127b53-d3c3-43db-b17b-a7305ed990c1",
                      "text": "<p>Loss of data entered by users</p>",
                      "effects": "<p>Users stop using the application</p>",
                      "severity": 6,
                      "type": "FAIL",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "40",
                          "guid": "fd9820d7-ae42-411a-8662-542b1328fbbb",
                          "text": "<p>The application crashes due to a bug</p>",
                          "detectability": 8,
                          "detection": "<p>Stability test of the application with corner case data.</p>",
                          "probability": 3,
                          "severity": 6,
                          "type": "CAUSE",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "id": "26",
                              "guid": "0a3c9583-0ed9-444c-ba41-ec92411357a5",
                              "text": "<p>Implement <em>Autosave</em> functionality storing immediately all changes into a persistent application storage so that only the last unsaved change is lost.</p>",
                              "detectability": 8,
                              "probability": 3,
                              "responsibility": "Libor Bus",
                              "severity": 2,
                              "targetDate": "2015-12-31",
                              "type": "ACT"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "id": "44",
                          "guid": "1df2d01c-25bd-42e0-8b67-ae56c3345ddd",
                          "text": "<p>Functional bug in user data handling</p>",
                          "detectability": 4,
                          "detection": "<p>Unit tests of user data handling with 90% coverage.</p>",
                          "probability": 3,
                          "severity": 6,
                          "type": "CAUSE",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "id": "45",
                              "guid": "ca3122fe-35fd-4b92-bb92-e05cdd01e4d7",
                              "text": "<p>Unit tests with 99% coverage</p>",
                              "detectability": 1,
                              "probability": 3,
                              "responsibility": "Libor Bus",
                              "severity": 6,
                              "targetDate": "2018-09-30",
                              "type": "ACT"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "37",
          "guid": "1d2eccc0-4739-4c29-9e66-03dd9e28d9e4",
          "heading": "References",
          "type": "SEC",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "38",
              "guid": "cf880862-c782-47de-a092-07d3f5933ddc",
              "text": "<p><strong>[DEMO-NEEDS]:</strong> ReqView User Needs</p>",
              "type": "INF"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "attributes": {
